<section id="plugins">
<h3>Integrations</h3>

<p>Everything here is optional. The Unified Grader looks for each plugin when it needs it, and
hides the matching part of the screen when the plugin is not there.</p>

<div class="local-unifiedgrader-help-table local-unifiedgrader-help-table-stack">
<table class="table-reboot">
    <thead><tr><th scope="col">If you want</th><th scope="col">You need</th><th scope="col">Details</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr><th scope="row">Annotation of Word files and online text</th><td data-label="You need">A document converter enabled in Moodle</td><td><a href="#plugin-converter">Document conversion</a></td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Automatic late penalties</th><td data-label="You need">Moodle's grade penalty rules</td><td><a href="#plugin-gradepenalty-duedate">Late penalty rules</a></td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Plagiarism results in the grader</th><td data-label="You need">Any Moodle plagiarism plugin</td><td><a href="#plugin-plagiarism">Plagiarism</a></td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Proctoring review priority</th><td data-label="You need">The Moodle plugin of Quilgo, ProctorLink, AutoProctor or SMOWL</td><td><a href="#admin-proctoring">Proctoring setup</a></td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">BigBlueButton engagement figures and rubrics</th><td data-label="You need">Session summaries from the BigBlueButton server; the advanced grading extension for rubrics</td><td><a href="#plugin-advgrd">BigBlueButton setup</a></td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Recorded audio and video feedback</th><td data-label="You need">A recorder plugin for the TinyMCE editor</td><td><a href="#plugin-tinymce-recorder">Recording</a></td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Portfolio submissions, translation</th><td data-label="You need">The Byblos or <code>local_nida</code> plugins</td><td><a href="#plugin-byblos">Other integrations</a></td></tr>
    </tbody>
</table>
</div>

{{! ----- Document conversion ----- }}
<section id="plugin-converter">
<h4>Document conversion</h4>
<p>The grader shows Word and other office files, and online text, as PDFs so that teachers can
annotate them. It asks Moodle to convert them, through whichever document converter is enabled
in Moodle (<strong>Site administration &gt; Plugins &gt; Document converters</strong>). The
Unified Grader has no converter of its own.</p>
<ul>
    <li>Without a converter, PDFs and images can still be annotated. Office files can be downloaded, and online text shows inline.</li>
    <li>Online text is converted only when <em>Render online text as PDF</em> is on (<a href="#settings-grading">Grading settings</a>).</li>
    <li>When a conversion fails, the teacher sees <em>This file could not be converted to PDF for preview.</em> and a <strong>Retry conversion</strong> button, which discards the failed attempt and asks again.</li>
</ul>
<p>If conversions fail while the converter is running, see
<a href="#ts-conversion-port">Troubleshooting</a>.</p>
</section>

{{! ----- Late penalty rules ----- }}
<section id="plugin-gradepenalty-duedate">
<h4>Late penalty rules</h4>
<p>On Moodle 5.3 the Unified Grader applies late penalties itself, to assignments, forums and
quizzes alike. The <em>rules</em> (how much to deduct for how late) are Moodle's own due date
penalty rules (<code>gradepenalty_duedate</code>, part of Moodle), set for the site, a course or
an activity under Moodle's grade penalty settings. The most specific rule wins.</p>
<ul>
    <li>Each activity opts in with its own <strong>Apply late penalties</strong> tick box.</li>
    <li>The grade a teacher gives stays the raw grade. The deduction is recorded beside it in the
        gradebook, which shows its penalty icon. Nothing is fixed with an override, so regrades and new attempts carry through.</li>
    <li>Penalties are applied again whenever a grade is saved anywhere in Moodle, a quiz is regraded, or a due date, extension or override changes.</li>
    <li>Other penalties that teachers add in the grader work without any rules.</li>
</ul>

<div class="local-unifiedgrader-help-note local-unifiedgrader-help-note-warn">
    <p><strong>Take Assignment out of Moodle's own penalties.</strong> While <em>Assignment</em>
    is ticked under <em>Grade penalties: supported modules</em>, Moodle still penalises assignments
    that have its own <em>Apply penalties</em> setting on, and the Unified Grader stands back for
    those so that nothing is deducted twice. They then behave differently from forums and quizzes.
    The Grading settings page shows a warning with a link while this is the case.</p>
</div>

<p id="plugin-quizaccess-duedate"><strong>Upgrading from an older Moodle.</strong> Before Moodle
5.3, quiz due dates came from the <code>quizaccess_duedate</code> access rule. That rule is now
legacy: Moodle 5.3 has the quiz due date in core, and the Unified Grader ignores the rule there
even if it is still installed. Before you uninstall it, let the hourly task
<em>migrate_penalties</em> run once, or run
<code>php local/unifiedgrader/cli/migrate_penalties.php</code>, so that quizzes which had late
penalties switched on keep them.</p>
</section>

{{! ----- Plagiarism ----- }}
<section id="plugin-plagiarism">
<h4>Plagiarism</h4>
<p>The grader shows whatever the site's plagiarism plugin returns for a file, an online text or a
forum post. It does not contact any plagiarism service itself and has no plagiarism settings.</p>
<ul>
    <li>Plagiarism plugins must be enabled in Moodle's advanced features, and one must be set up for the activity.</li>
    <li>Scores, colours, pending and error states, and the link to the full report are the plugin's own.</li>
    <li>With no result there is no Plagiarism card, and the integrity button moves to the grade card.</li>
    <li>The optional report form is set under <a href="#settings-integrity">Academic integrity</a>. It can be any web form that accepts values in its address.</li>
</ul>
</section>

{{! ----- Proctoring ----- }}
<section id="admin-proctoring">
<h4>Proctoring setup <span class="local-unifiedgrader-help-new">New in 3.0</span></h4>

<ol>
    <li>Install and set up the proctoring service's own Moodle plugin. The grader reads its results through that plugin and never asks for connection details a second time.</li>
    <li>Under <a href="#settings-integrity">Academic integrity</a>, tick the service in <em>Proctoring services to show</em> and save.</li>
    <li>Adjust the service's settings, which now appear on the same page.</li>
    <li>Check that the people who should see results hold <code>local/unifiedgrader:viewproctoring</code>.</li>
</ol>
<p>There is nothing to set on each quiz. A quiz shows results when the service's plugin is in use for it.</p>

<div class="local-unifiedgrader-help-table local-unifiedgrader-help-table-stack">
<table class="table-reboot">
    <thead><tr><th scope="col">Service</th><th scope="col">Moodle plugin</th><th scope="col">How the colour is decided</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <th scope="row">Quilgo</th>
            <td data-label="Moodle plugin"><code>quizaccess_quilgo</code></td>
            <td>Quilgo's own confidence level: high is green, moderate is yellow, low is red. One result per attempt. No settings here.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <th scope="row">ProctorLink</th>
            <td data-label="Moodle plugin"><code>quizaccess_quizproctoring</code></td>
            <td>By the kind of warning, not the number: any warning ticked as high priority is red, any other is yellow, none is green. One result per attempt.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <th scope="row">AutoProctor</th>
            <td data-label="Moodle plugin"><code>quizaccess_autoproctor</code></td>
            <td>By its trust score against two thresholds: 80% and above is green, 50% and above is yellow, lower is red, unless you change them. One result per attempt.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <th scope="row">SMOWL</th>
            <td data-label="Moodle plugin"><code>block_smowl</code></td>
            <td>By the kind of alarm: any alarm ticked as high priority is red, any other is yellow, none is green. One result per student per quiz.</td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>
</div>

<ul>
    <li><strong>SMOWL needs two things:</strong> the SMOWL block in the course, and the quiz switched on in the SMOWL panel. The grader uses the connection details saved in the SMOWL plugin. A course without the block is never asked about.</li>
    <li><strong>Pending evidence is never shown as low priority.</strong> Until the service has finished, a student with nothing against them shows <em>Awaiting review</em>. An alarm already reported counts at once and is marked provisional.</li>
    <li><strong>Links</strong> open the service's own report in a new tab, for users who hold that plugin's report capability.</li>
    <li><strong>Load:</strong> answers fetched from a service are kept for fifteen minutes. The grader draws first and asks afterwards, so an unreachable service does not hold up marking.</li>
    <li>The grader only reads the other plugins' data. It never writes to it.</li>
</ul>
</section>

{{! ----- BigBlueButton ----- }}
<section id="plugin-advgrd">
<h4>BigBlueButton setup</h4>
<div class="local-unifiedgrader-help-table local-unifiedgrader-help-table-stack">
<table class="table-reboot">
    <thead><tr><th scope="col">Where</th><th scope="col">Setting</th><th scope="col">Why</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr><th scope="row">Unified Grader</th><td data-label="Setting"><code>enable_bigbluebuttonbn</code></td><td>BigBlueButton activities open in the grader.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Moodle's BigBlueButton plugin</th><td data-label="Setting"><em>Register live sessions</em></td><td>Tells the BigBlueButton server to send a summary to Moodle when a session ends. Activity Points come from it.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">BigBlueButton server</th><td data-label="Setting"><code>defaultKeepEvents=true</code></td><td>The server keeps the events the summary is built from.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Network</th><td data-label="Setting">The server reachable from Moodle</td><td>For recordings, and for <strong>Refresh attendance</strong>.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
</table>
</div>
<ul>
    <li>Summaries are only sent for sessions started after the settings are on. For earlier
        recordings, <strong>Refresh attendance</strong> reads attendance from each recording. Run
        it once per activity after upgrading, and when a recording is added. The same can be done
        for the whole site with <code>php local/unifiedgrader/cli/refresh_bbb_engagement.php --all</code> (<code>--help</code> lists the options).</li>
    <li>While <em>Register live sessions</em> is off, the grader says so. Administrators get a link to the setting.</li>
    <li>With the <code>bbbext_advgrd</code> extension installed, a rubric or marking guide set on a
        BigBlueButton activity appears in the grader, and the extension's own player with its
        comment timeline takes the place of the plain recording.</li>
</ul>
</section>

{{! ----- Recorder ----- }}
<section id="plugin-tinymce-recorder">
<h4>Recording audio and video feedback</h4>
<p>The feedback editor is Moodle's TinyMCE editor. If a recorder plugin for TinyMCE is installed,
its buttons appear in the editor and teachers can record feedback. The Unified Grader has no
recorder of its own. Teachers whose preferred editor is not TinyMCE get a plain text box for
comments on quiz questions.</p>
</section>

{{! ----- Byblos, nida ----- }}
<section id="plugin-byblos">
<h4>Other integrations</h4>
<p><strong>Byblos portfolio.</strong> When an assignment accepts Byblos portfolio submissions, the
portfolio shows in the preview with a button to open it in its own window, and a
<em>Portfolio</em> pill beside any files the student also attached.</p>

<p id="plugin-nida"><strong>Translation (<code>local_nida</code>).</strong> In courses enabled for
it, the grader can show a machine translation of a submission beside the original, lets the marker
confirm the submission's language, and lets them comment on a single phrase of the text. Students
then read their feedback in their own language. Without the plugin, or in a course that is not
enabled, none of this appears.</p>
</section>

{{! ----- Scheduled tasks ----- }}
<section id="admin-tasks">
<h4>Scheduled tasks</h4>
<div class="local-unifiedgrader-help-table local-unifiedgrader-help-table-stack">
<table class="table-reboot">
    <thead><tr><th scope="col">Task</th><th scope="col">Runs</th><th scope="col">What it does</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr><th scope="row"><code>open_friction</code></th><td data-label="Runs">Daily</td><td>Releases marks that Friction Feedback has held past either time limit.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row"><code>expire_forum_extensions</code></th><td data-label="Runs">Every 15 minutes</td><td>Ends a student's access to post in a forum after its cut-off once their extension is over, and starts it where a cut-off was moved inside an extension already granted. See <a href="#feature-overrides">Dates and extensions</a>.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row"><code>migrate_penalties</code></th><td data-label="Runs">Hourly, once</td><td>On Moodle 5.3, keeps the late penalty switch each quiz had under the legacy quiz due date rule.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row"><code>resync_penalties</code></th><td data-label="Runs">When needed</td><td>Recalculates an activity's penalties after its settings change.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
</table>
</div>
<p>All three need Moodle's cron to be running.</p>
</section>

</section>
